# Renderer — Vector Rendering Layer

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `renderer.py` | `CrossSectionRenderer` facade; dispatches to layout mixins |
| `renderer_common.py` | `RendererGeometryMixin` — wells, profile lookup, style resolution |
| `renderer_section_sheet.py` | `SectionSheetLayoutMixin` — Strater-like section sheet |
| `renderer_chart.py` | `ChartLayoutMixin` — legacy debug chart |
| `renderer_consulting.py` | `ConsultingLayoutMixin` — report sheet, title block, screens/gradients |

Input: `GeologicalPolygon` list, projected DataFrame, optional `WaterLevel` / screens / gradients / `EnvironmentalReading`.
Output: Matplotlib figure or SVG/PNG/PDF bytes.

**No projection or pinch-out logic** — consume pre-built polygons and projected intervals only.
Lithology fills use the **BH Log** legend (Excel → `constants.get_lithology_style()`; namespaced as `USGS_LITHOLOGY_*`).

`CrossSectionRenderer` accepts `environmental_readings` plus `environmental_parameters` (filter names). When profile `show_parameter_markers` is on, `_draw_parameter_readings()` / `parameter_marker` place labels (pipeline forces markers on when `environmental_parameters` is non-empty).

## Render Profiles (`render_profiles.py`)

`CrossSectionRenderProfile` controls layout without a second renderer:

| Field | Section sheet (default) | Consulting section | Chart (legacy) |
|-------|-------------------------|-------------------|----------------|
| `layout` | `section_sheet` | `consulting_section` | `chart` |
| `track_width_m` | 3.0 | 1.2 (white columns) | 1.6 |
| `show_track_lithology` | true | false | true |
| `show_grid` / `show_report_grid` | false | report grid (1 m / 10 m) | true |
| `show_ground_surface` / `show_sky_fill` | true / true | true / false | false |
| `show_contact_ticks` / `show_eol_bar` / `show_track_border` | true | false | false |
| `show_column_headers` | true | false (IDs above plot) | false |
| `show_dual_y_axes` | false | true | false |
| `legend_in_title_block` | false | true | false |
| `y_axis_mode` | `elevation_rl` or `depth_below_collar` | `elevation_rl` | `elevation_rl` |
| `water_symbol` | triangle | triangle (labeled RL) | circle |
| `title_block` / `show_ve_annotation` | footer metadata / in-plot | subtitle band + footer legend | false |

Wire profile via `pipeline.build_cross_section(render_layout=..., elevation_mode=...)` or `CrossSectionRenderer(render_profile=...)`.
Theme colors live in `render_theme.py`.

## Interpretation Modes

| Mode | Polygons | Inter-hole fill | Disclaimer |
|------|----------|-----------------|------------|
| `interpolated` | Yes | Filled fence diagram | "Interpreted fence diagram — contacts are linear…" |
| `correlation_lines` | Yes | Contact lines only (no fill) | Correlation-lines disclaimer |
| `borehole_only` | Empty list | None | "Observed borehole data only — no inter-borehole correlation." |

Set via `CrossSectionRenderer(interpretation_mode=...)` or `pipeline.build_cross_section(interpretation_mode=...)`.

## Section-Sheet Layers (z-order, Strater-like)

1. **Uncertainty zones** — amber shading when spacing/offset thresholds exceeded (bottom-most, zorder 0)
2. **Sky fill** — light fill above interpolated ground surface (`show_sky_fill`)
3. **Fence polygons** — BH Log colors/hatches; lower alpha (`fence_alpha` ~0.58) so tracks read in front
4. **Track lithology** — wide bordered rectangles per interval inside each borehole track
5. **Track borders** — white column outline from collar to TD
6. **Contact ticks** — horizontal lines at interval tops/bottoms across track width
7. **Deviated centerlines** — dotted polyline through interval midpoints when deviation survey present
8. **Raster log strips** — optional hatched placeholder column (`RasterLogStrip` model); drawn with default patch zorder 1, so it sits beneath fence polygons and track lithology; `image_bytes` is defined but not yet rendered
9. **Ground surface** — thick green/brown polyline
10. **Water table** — symbol per hole (circle/triangle/diamond) + optional dashed interpolation
11. **EOL bars** — horizontal end-of-log marker at TD
12. **Column headers** — hole ID, RL or depth label, TD per track (below the plot in `elevation_rl` mode; above it in `depth_below_collar` mode)
13. **Faults / unconformities / parameter markers** (`_draw_parameter_readings`, filtered by `environmental_parameters`)
14. **Overlap markers** — when `overlap_pairs` provided
15. **Scale bar** + **VE annotation** (`V.E. N×`)
16. **Legend** — lithology codes (when `show_legend=True`)
17. **Title block footer** — disclaimer + `SectionFigureMetadata` (CRS, datum, azimuth, VE, hole count)

## Chart Layout (legacy debug)

Thin center sticks, optional dashed grid, floating bbox labels, no sky/EOL/contact ticks. Use `CHART_PROFILE` or `render_layout="chart"`.

## Consulting Section Layout (EcoVenture-style report sheet)

Fence-first layout matching consulting cross-section figures (`render_layout="consulting_section"`). Uses `GridSpec` `height_ratios=[58, 12, 22]`: plot (~63%), subtitle band (~13%), simplified title block (~24%).

**Plot layers (z-order):**

1. **Report grid** — 1 m elevation / 10 m distance majors (20 m when span > 200 m); dual **ELEVATION ABOVE SEA LEVEL (MASL)** axes (profile `y_axis_label`; `ELEVATION (m)` is the last-resort fallback)
2. **Fence polygons** — opaque fills (`fence_alpha=1.0`); no wide track lithology
3. **Ground surface** — interpolated collar polyline (no sky fill)
4. **Well columns** — narrow filled rectangles collar to TD via `_draw_well_columns` (`TRACK_FILL_COLOR`); `_draw_thin_well_sticks` exists but is unused
5. **Screen intervals** — opaque `TRACK_FILL_COLOR` + `hatch="///"` (Matplotlib needs a non-transparent face for hatch); legend swatch matches
6. **Gradients** — vertical arrows when provided
7. **Hole ID labels** — above each stick
8. **Transect end labels** — optional via `ConsultingTitleBlock`
9. **Water table** — labeled RL at each ▼; solid interpolation line when ≥2 points (`water_line_solid=True`)
10. **Faults / unconformities / parameter markers** (`_draw_parameter_readings` when `show_parameter_markers`)

**Subtitle band:** section label, `SCALE {map_scale}`, `{VE}× VERTICAL EXAGGERATION`, graphic scale bar.

**Title block:** lithology swatches + GW symbol key + project metadata (`ConsultingTitleBlock` via `SectionBuildRequest.consulting_title_block`).

Wire via `pipeline.build_cross_section(render_layout="consulting_section", consulting_title_block=...)`.
Streamlit: sidebar **Output style** selectbox preset **Consulting report (title block)** + **Consulting report sheet** expander.

## Visual Requirements

- Fill polygons via `matplotlib.collections.PolyCollection` using `constants.get_lithology_style()` (BH Log palette)
- User overrides via `paths.lithology_styles_path()` (user data dir, not repo `data/`)
- Expose **`vertical_exaggeration`** (Y-axis multiplier) and **`scale_bar_length_m`**
- Hatch patterns toggled via `show_hatches`

## Y-Axis Modes

- `elevation_rl` — absolute reduced level (default)
- `depth_below_collar` — inverted depth axis; wired from UI `elevation_mode=relative`

## Export

- `to_svg_bytes()` / `to_png_bytes(dpi=300)` on rendered figure
- `export_figure_bytes(figure, export_formats, ...)` — single figure, selective encoding via `export_formats`
- `pipeline.build_cross_section(export_formats=...)` returns SVG/PNG/PDF bytes per format set (default `{"svg"}` for tests)
- Streamlit Generate: `cached_build_section()` is **SVG-only**; primary Prepare PNG & PDF via `cached_build_section_exports()`; secondary per-format via `cached_build_section_png` / `cached_build_section_pdf`
- `report_export.export_section_pdf()` — page 1 section, page 2 legend/metadata/QA summary; reuses `section_figure` when provided
- Allowed: import stratigraphy **types** (`GeologicalPolygon`, `PolygonOverlap`) — not correlation/pinch-out logic
